        <object placeholders="1" c4Name="PKCE Security Enhancements" c4Type="SecurityNote" c4Description="✅ Code Challenge/Verifier prevents authorization code interception&#xa;✅ Direct Access Grants disabled (no Resource Owner Password Flow)&#xa;✅ SHA256 hashing for code challenge method (S256)&#xa;✅ Silent SSO for seamless user experience&#xa;✅ Public client without client secret requirement&#xa;✅ Protection against CSRF and code injection attacks" label="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;%c4Name%&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px&quot;&gt;%c4Description%&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" id="pkce-security">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=none;fillColor=#f0f0f0;fontColor=#333333;align=left;arcSize=10;strokeColor=#666666;metaEdit=1;resizable=0;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="160" width="400" x="80" y="1640" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </object>
        <object placeholders="1" c4Name="PKCE Flow Implementation" c4Type="TechnicalNote" c4Description="1. Client generates code_verifier (43-128 random characters)&#xa;2. Client creates code_challenge = SHA256(code_verifier)&#xa;3. Authorization request includes code_challenge + method=S256&#xa;4. Token exchange includes code_verifier for validation&#xa;5. Server verifies: SHA256(code_verifier) == code_challenge&#xa;6. Framework: @react-keycloak/web with pkceMethod: &#39;S256&#39;" label="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;%c4Name%&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px&quot;&gt;%c4Description%&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" id="pkce-implementation">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=none;fillColor=#e1d5e7;fontColor=#333333;align=left;arcSize=10;strokeColor=#9673a6;metaEdit=1;resizable=0;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="160" width="400" x="600" y="1640" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </object>
